// /updates: What's new, the changelog of the course. Every update is a short lesson under it (content/updates/*.flecs,
// /updates/<slug>) with Update {date, version, line, glyph}: what changed in blaze, said in the lesson format, on the
// course path next to the lesson it extends ((Requires, ...)) and in the band of its channel ((InTheme, ...)). This
// page lists them newest first (UpdateLog, renderer core render.rs); client/learn.ts marks the ones published since
// the reader's last visit New, and the sidebar row counts them (client/side.ts).
// An update is a user-visible change to blaze, not to this site. Keep each one small: three to five steps, one or two
// questions, and a closing line with its pull requests.
site {
  updates : Page {
    Narrow
    Title: {"What's new"}
    Nav: {"What's new", -1}
    Icon: {"sparkle"}
    (InGroup, nav.learn)
    Description: {"What has changed in blaze, as short lessons on the course: newest first, with the ones new since your last visit marked."}
    Lede lede("What has changed in blaze, newest first. Each update is a short lesson that extends one on the [course](/), and sits next to it on the path.")
    Dim channels("Updates tagged Canary are in canary releases or behind an experimental flag; the rest are on stable. [Install](/install) says how to pick a channel.")
    UpdateLog log
    Dim kept("Which updates are new is worked out in this browser, from when you last came by. Nothing is sent anywhere.")
  }
}
